"
Whether the backend skips its syntax and compile checks of methods, true only while it applies text the image rendered itself: a restore, a rollback or a moved extension. That text holds the methods the image already has, and from Pharo 14 the image may hold one with a compile error, which the checks would refuse.

A process variable, since requests arrive on several server processes at once.
"
Class {
	#name : 'PIFSMethodChecksSkipped',
	#superclass : 'DynamicVariable',
	#category : 'PharoImageFS',
	#package : 'PharoImageFS'
}

{ #category : 'accessing' }
PIFSMethodChecksSkipped >> default [

	^ false
]
